  "title": "falcodump: Exit with success if there are no interfaces",
  "description": "The tests expect a successful return code even if there are on\ninterfaces (even if the \"always_present\" is false.) That's what\nandroiddump does.\n\nBoth should perhaps return a special exit code for no interfaces\n(WS_EXIT_NO_INTERFACES), though the extcap tests harness would need\nto be changed to allow that exit code when no interfaces are\nallowed.\n\nThis keeps tests from failing, e.g. on the Windows packages.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4caad1c2dde20c10dc96d9eb29aac8f2d0cf37c2)",
